{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"# Live rich-text cutover + state echo suppression + concurrency conflict safety\n\n## Context / Problem\nCut the live Cloud and DC send paths to the rich codecs (needs `e59d`, `271c`), echo-safely.\nDC's codec is lossy/one-way, so `decode(encode(x))==x` cannot gate loops; echo suppression is\nby **state**: current Jira value vs last-synced baseline (ADR 0026; `binding_store.get_baseline`\n`:447` / `set_baseline` `:450`; `_BASELINE_FIELDS` in `peer_state.py:37`).\n\n**Reused unchanged:** ADR-0026/d6bd baseline diff (`binding_store.get_baseline` via\n`InboundMapper`, `outbound_field_diff.py:265`; `description` in `_INBOUND_MIRRORED_FIELDS` `:47`,\nvia `_compute_field_changes`); once-only re-emit convergence requires the codec law\n`normalize_outbound(t) == decode_inbound(to_wire(t))` (`test_rich_text_codec.py:163`, a32a)\nplus round-trip idempotence (100.00% on the 360-body Cloud corpus). **The non-idempotent tail is bounded.** Consecutiveness is PERSISTED, not inferred: the\ninline binding record carries a change-gated `rich_reemit` counter beside `rich_sha`,\nincremented when a field is emitted with `rich_sha` unchanged and reset to 0 when\n`rich_sha` changes or the baseline refreshes — so it stays 0 (no churn) on healthy\nbodies. At `rich_reemit == 2` do ONE post-push GET for that field and hand the result to\n`_advance_baselines` (`reconcile_helpers.py:602`, `ctx.curr_snapshot`) as a\n`synced_fields` overlay via `binding_store.merge_baseline` (`:453`), so\n`_advance_baselines` REMAINS the sole baseline writer. Comment dedup\n(`outbound_comments.py:48`) intact.\n\n## The live cutover\n- **Cloud:** point the four `AdfCodec` ops at `adf.py`'s Markdown-aware fns\n  (`to_wire→markdown_to_adf`, `decode_inbound→adf_to_markdown`,\n  `normalize_outbound→adf_to_markdown∘markdown_to_adf`, `fit_outbound→fit_markdown_to_adf_limit`)\n  + whole-codec plain-text fallback; pin test `test_rich_text_codec.py:198/205/207/208`. Reroute:\n  encode `adapters/jira/acli.py:209`, `acli_cli_ops.py:386`; fit `jira_fields.py:53`; compares\n  `adf.normalize_description`/`adf.fit_text_to_adf_limit` (`outbound_fields.py:586`,\n  `inbound_differ.py:210`) — **send-fit and compare-fit must be one transform**.\n- **DC:** `WikiTextCodec.to_wire` delegates to `wiki_render.render_markdown_to_wiki` (`271c`);\n  **redefine `WikiTextCodec.normalize_outbound` to `decode_inbound(to_wire(t))`**, restoring the\n  codec law. Send composes `normalize_outbound(fit_outbound(value))` (`outbound_mapper.py:77`)\n  → rendered wiki on `issue.update(fields=…)`. **TWO other DC send sites:**\n  `_map_local_to_dc_fields` (`adapters/jira_datacenter/backend.py:57`) AND\n  `adapters/jira_datacenter/_issues.py`, with its OWN\n  `_DESCRIPTION_CODEC = WikiTextCodec()` (`:40`) applying only `fit_outbound` WITHOUT `to_wire`\n  (`:111`) — BOTH must route through `to_wire` (render before the fit) or they ship un-rendered\n  Markdown. Retarget DC pin tests (`test_wiki_normalize_is_identity`,\n  `test_wiki_codec_wire_shape_and_decode_are_the_plain_string`,\n  `test_non_string_values_pass_through_untouched`).\n\n## Design decisions\n1. **Two DISTINCT compares — do not collapse.** *Emit (`outbound_field_diff.py:288`),\n   local-vs-REMOTE — UNCHANGED:* `normalize_outbound(fit_outbound(local))` vs\n   `canonical_remote[\"description\"]` = `decode_inbound(remote_wire)`\n   (`inbound_mapper.map_remote_to_local`); both decoded → lossy round-trip cancels; an\n   un-normalized remote forces the one-time legacy re-emit (`outbound_fields.py:586`).\n   *Baseline (`_suppressed_by_inbound` `:323`, `_local_matches_baseline` `:464`) — LOCAL side\n   normalized:* raw local Markdown vs `decode(baseline_wire)` differ in space → \"local changed\"\n   every pass; route the local side through `RichTextCodec.normalize_outbound`\n   (`decode∘to_wire`, via `OutboundFieldMapper.map_fields_to_remote`), sole normalizer.\n   `_remote_matches_baseline` (`:399`) — UNCHANGED.\n2. **Concurrent both-sides edit — unchanged (a713 local-wins).** Both differing from `baseline` →\n   `outbound_field_diff.py:450-457` appends `(jira_key, fname)` to `conflict_sink`;\n   `run_differs.py:_emit_outbound_field_alerts` (`:97`) emits the deduped alert. Emit stays\n   local-wins; inbound description stays **additive**\n   (`conflict_resolver.FIELD_CLASSES`/`_field_contract.FIELD_CONTRACT`, `resolve_additive`).\n3. **Shared-op side effect.** The redefinition also reaches the DC\n   comment-diff dedup key (`outbound_comments._diff_comments` via `_resolve_codec:123`, `:286`;\n   `_IdentityCodec` docstring `:106-116`); that path keeps the identity/plain normalizer UNCHANGED.\n4. **Origin-gating + churn.** Updates fire only when `local != baseline`, so a Jira-authored\n   construct (panel/mention/date, decoded by `adf.py` `:164/219`) survives an edit-free pass.\n   Store a change-gated `rich_sha = sha256(rendered_wire)[:16]` (8 bytes) **inline** in the binding\n   (0.07 KB/version; a per-pass timestamp reproduced `0303`'s 12.62 KB anti-pattern); the compare\n   never writes back.\n\n## Scope (IN)\n- `adapters/jira/rich_text_codec.py` (+ fallback), `adapters/jira_family/rich_text.py`, Cloud\n  consumer sites above, `backend.py` (`:57`) CREATE path — gated.\n- **Cutover flag (NEW config surface, defaults OFF):** `reconciler.rich_text_cutover`\n  (`off`|`cloud`|`dc`|`both`), four-file surface: `_config_schema.py` (field +\n  validator), `_config_sources.py` (auto-derived\n  `REBAR_RECONCILER_RICH_TEXT_CUTOVER`), `tests/golden/config_surface.json`\n  (regenerate), `docs/config.md`. Gates codec selection on BOTH send paths; off =\n  plain/identity wire (the rollback; no capability revert). Enable per client, Cloud then DC,\n  after canary.\n- `binding_store.py` inline `rich_sha`; `outbound_field_diff.py` (`:323`, `:464`) local-side normalize\n  only (`:292`, `_apply_mutations` untouched); tests under `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/`.\n\n## Scope (OUT)\n- No new three-way merge, LWW clock, conflict sink, or parallel `norm()`; no change to\n  `FIELD_CLASSES`/`_field_contract` or `inbound_fields.normalize_rich_text`; comment rendering and\n  the DC comment dedup-key migration (`789c`).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Cloud: a converted ADF description posts once; a second pass emits zero updates\n  (`test_cloud_cutover_converges`).\n- [ ] DC: `issue.update(fields=…)` gets rendered wiki, not raw Markdown; a second pass emits\n  zero updates (`test_dc_cutover_converges`).\n- [ ] TWO distinct compares: emit on the plain inbound-decoded remote; baseline compares'\n  LOCAL side through `normalize_outbound` to match `decode(baseline_wire)`; a no-edit body stays\n  suppressed across passes, a rebar edit shows changed, a legacy body upgrades once then converges (`test_lossy_baseline_compare_local_normalized`,\n  `test_legacy_body_upgrades_once`, `test_lossy_body_converges_across_passes`).\n- [ ] The `WikiTextCodec.normalize_outbound` redefinition leaves the DC comment-diff dedup key\n  unshifted; comment-diff converges with no duplicate re-post\n  (`test_dc_comment_diff_unchanged_by_cutover`).\n- [ ] Outbound fires only on a rebar-originated change (`local != baseline`); the baseline\n  advances via `_advance_baselines`; a benign re-canonicalization converges in one re-emit, no re-GET (`test_echo_rebar_origin_only`, `test_recanonicalization_converges`).\n- [ ] A Jira-authored construct (panel/mention/date) survives a later rebar pass under\n  origin-gating (`test_jira_native_construct_survives`).\n- [ ] A concurrent both-sides body edit keeps rebar's body (local-wins) AND raises the\n  `outbound-field-conflict` alert, recording the remote value (`test_concurrent_conflict_alerts`).\n- [ ] An inline change-gated 8-byte `rich_sha` is stored, no per-pass timestamp, changing 0\n  entries on a no-op pass; the git-delta harness verifies ≤0.07 KB/version.\n- [ ] Flag-gated, defaults OFF (opt-in per client, not a 100%-traffic flip), reverting to the\n  plain/identity wire when off (`test_cutover_defaults_off`,\n  `test_cutover_rollback_restores_plain`).\n- [ ] With the marklas extra absent, the cutover path emits the plain-text ADF wire (today's\n  behaviour), raising nothing; a test simulates the ImportError with the flag ON."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786600275391405001,"uuid":"044bf370-e1ea-4481-a6cd-4b5752e0ca7c"}